These skills enforce discipline, and discipline holds until someone leans on it. Run each
in a **fresh session** with the skill installed. A session that just wrote the skill will
pass by accident.

{{EVAL_PROMPTS}}

## Reading the results

A failure is the skill's fault, not the agent's. When one fails, capture the exact wording
the agent used to justify itself and add it to the `Rationalizations` table as a new row.
That verbatim phrasing is worth more than anything you'd invent — it's the loophole that
actually exists.

Re-run after editing. A rule that survives three pressure prompts is worth trusting; one
that has never been pushed on is a hypothesis.

Update **Last run** to today's date once you've actually run all three, pass or fail — it's
the one signal that tells a later reader (or `/skill:project-init`, on a re-run) whether this
skill's discipline claims were ever tested or are still just asserted.
